This is actually a much better and more realistic workflow than only allowing the admin to add members. It gives your project more functionality while still letting the admin control who becomes a member.

Below is a clear prompt you can add to your main project requirements.

Member Registration & Approval System Prompt
======================================================
ONLINE MEMBER REGISTRATION & APPROVAL SYSTEM
======================================================

The Gym-Pro website should provide TWO methods to add new members.

---------------------------------------------
METHOD 1 : Online Registration Request
---------------------------------------------

A visitor who is NOT an existing member can click the "Register" button on the public website.

The visitor is NOT immediately considered a gym member.

Instead, they submit a membership request.

The registration form should collect:

• Full Name
• Gender
• Date of Birth
• Phone Number
• Email Address
• Address
• Emergency Contact
• Preferred Membership Plan
      - Standard
      - Premium
      - Elite
• Membership Duration
      - 1 Month
      - 3 Months
      - 6 Months
      - 12 Months
• Username
• Password

When the user clicks "Submit Request":

✔ Save all details into a database table named:

requested_members

Default Status:

Pending

No member account should become active immediately.

The visitor should see:

"Your membership request has been submitted successfully.
Our team will contact you shortly."

----------------------------------------------------
ADMIN REQUEST MANAGEMENT
----------------------------------------------------

The Admin Dashboard must include a new sidebar menu:

Member Requests

